# Wedding Site — Cursor Rules

You are helping build a **static, read-only** Next.js wedding site. Canonical product/engineering docs: **`README.md`**, **`docs/PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md`**, **`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`**, **`docs/VISUAL_QA.md`**, and numbered specs **`00`**–**`12`** (some contain historical framing—defer to **`README.md`** when they conflict).

## Critical constraints

Never create:

- ❌ RSVP page or RSVP workflow
- ❌ Attendance counting / guest tracking / confirmation flows
- ❌ Chatbot, AI chat widget, or chatbot SDK
- ❌ Public contact form or any `<form>` UX that collects guest data
- ❌ Public gallery upload
- ❌ Login / auth system
- ❌ Database
- ❌ API routes
- ❌ Server actions
- ❌ Middleware-based language routing / locale redirects
- ❌ Analytics in MVP

Guest support stays informational: deterministic FAQ plus **supporting LINE pages** documented in **`08_LINE_OA_RICH_MENU_SPEC.md`**—still **never** marketed as realtime AI concierge.

## Product truth — naming & locales

**Visible naming (bride-first):**

- `Tan & Top`
- `Narueporn & Theerut`

Never show groom-first order (`Top & Tan`, `Theerut & Narueporn`) in visible UI strings.

**Routing:**

- Thai default: `/`, `/schedule/`, `/venue/`, `/gallery/`, `/faq/`, `/line/`
- English: `/en`, `/en/schedule/`, `/en/venue/`, `/en/gallery/`, `/en/faq/`, `/en/line/`
- **`trailingSlash: true`** in production config — prefer links that match exported URLs.

**Do not restore** Accommodation or Dress-code routes/menus unless the product charter changes.

## Stack (see `package.json` for pinned versions)

- Next.js App Router (currently **16.2.x**), TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4
- **pnpm only** (`packageManager` field)
- `next/font/google` → Cormorant Garamond + Inter + **IBM Plex Sans Thai**
- `lucide-react`, `motion` (subtle, reduced-motion-safe)
- Static export (**`output: 'export'`**), **`images.unoptimized: true`**
- Playwright (**dev**) + `pnpm screenshots` for deterministic visual QA (see **`docs/VISUAL_QA.md`**)

Conditional GitHub Pages hosting:

```txt
GITHUB_PAGES=true → basePath "/top-tanly-wedding" + trailing assetPrefix (see next.config.ts)
```

## Files & conventions

- **Components:** PascalCase files, default export (`components/layout/*`, `components/sections/*`, `components/ui/*`).
- **Content:** camelCase TS modules exporting typed objects (`content/th/*.ts`, `content/en/*.ts`, **`content/schema.ts`**).
- **Utils / hooks:** `lib/*.ts`, `lib/hooks/use*.ts`.

## Rendering patterns

- Default **Server Components**. Add `"use client"` only for interactivity (`MobileMenu`, `Navbar` scroll tweaks, accordion/fade wrappers, motion).
- Components accept **`className`** merged with **`cn()`**.
- Buttons/links/interactive widgets need visible focus styling (`focus-visible:ring-*`).
- Prefer `next/image` with explicit dimensions or `fill` + `sizes` for real assets; placeholders use **`PlaceholderImage`**.

## Styling (`03_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`)

- Tailwind utilities + tokens from **`app/globals.css`** `@theme`.
- Palette tokens only (`cream`, `ivory`, `champagne`, `rose-deep`, …) — avoid random hex unless extending tokens deliberately.
- Border radii conventions: cards `rounded-2xl`, media `rounded-xl`, CTAs/tags `rounded-full`.
- Shadows only where spec calls for warm soft elevation.

### Animation posture

✅ Fade / soft upward reveal, gentle hover lift on decorative imagery, restrained button fades, accordion easing with readable content states.

⚠️ Flip/gimmick transitions only on ornamental Home/Gallery motifs—never for schedule facts or urgent venue instructions.

❌ Parallax loops, flashy 3D flips, marquees, autoplay gag animations, bouncing overshoot gimmicks—anything disrespecting **`prefers-reduced-motion`**.

Screenshots tooling may disable CSS animations for deterministic PNG QA—don't interpret that as license to spam motion in production UI.

## Content rules (`04_CONTENT_MODEL.md`)

- **Never hardcode copy in JSX.** Import from **`content/th/*`** / **`content/en/*`** only.
- Use placeholders responsibly—never fabricated confirmed operational claims.
- Friendly tone: warm, elegant, concise.
- Spelling **`Venue`**, never `Vanue`.

## Navigation UX

Never list **Home** as a bullet. Logo lockup anchors to **`/`** (Thai) or **`/en`** (English).

Main nav mirrors product:

- Thai: `กำหนดการ · สถานที่ · แกลเลอรี · คำถามที่พบบ่อย · EN`
- English: `Schedule · Venue · Gallery · FAQ · TH`

**LINE** stays ancillary (support pages + CTAs)—never co-equal with Schedule/Venue in **`Navbar.tsx`/`MobileMenu.tsx`**.

## LINE positioning

Maintain `/line` + `/en/line` informational pages about official updates/reminders/coordinator assistance. Copy must clarify manual/human pacing—**not** instantaneous AI concierge nor RSVP automation.

## Accessibility & responsiveness

Follow **`06_RESPONSIVE_UX_SPEC.md`** + **`10_ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA_QA.md`:**

- Tap targets ≥ 44×44 px equivalents.
- One `<h1>` per route, logical heading ladders.
- Contrast thresholds (WCAG-ish: ~4.5:1 body, ~3:1 large type).
- Test 375 / 390 / 430 / 768 widths before desktop polishing.

## What NOT to do (recap)

- ❌ Accommodation / Dress-code resurrected casually
- ❌ Hardcoded multilingual strings sprinkled in JSX
- ❌ Runtime data fetching powering guest-critical info
- ❌ Decorative motion that hides schedule/map clarity
- ❌ Middleware locale experiments breaking static exports

When instructions conflict across legacy markdown packs, escalate with the repo owner—or default to **`README.md` + `.cursor/rules/wedding-site.mdc`**.
